# Experiment proposals

This directory turns the geometric-control methods in this repository into
testable experiments.

## Current proposal

### [Single-qubit deterministic benchmarking (1qb-DB)](1qb-DB/)

The 1qb-DB experiment repeats \(X_\pi\)-pulse pairs to amplify coherent
pulse-area error. It compares a standard Gaussian pulse with a geometric pulse
designed to suppress multiplicative amplitude error.

An imperfect pulse produces an oscillation in the measured \(|0\rangle\)
survival probability. A successful robust pulse should strongly suppress that
oscillation over the tested range.

Current status:

- analytic Mathematica model: available;
- Gaussian and strictly resonant robust waveforms: validated for
  \(\pm3\%\) error through 60 cycles;
- waveform-level DB simulation: complete;
- hardware-unit conversion and experiment: planned.

See the [1qb-DB README](1qb-DB/) for the protocol and implementation plan.
